       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Sertraline 1000 mg/day is five times the labeled maximum of 200 mg/day. I can't verify the clinical rationale, and I know of no indication or treatment stage where this dose is appropriate. The risk is severe, and a daily order could be given repeatedly before anyone catches it.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **If the dose was a typo:** Give me the corrected dose, such as 100 mg or 200 mg PO once daily, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **If a higher-than-standard dose is intended:** Have a pharmacist or the attending verify it. Document the rationale, such as a specialist recommendation or a protocol. The order will likely need the hospital's override process.\n- **If a different drug or regimen was intended:** Tell me and I'll enter that instead.\n\nI can enter a dose within the approved range now if you'd like."
